From 351ac280f75cd36cbed27274a01cd2e05e2a246c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ikemen NX contributors <ikemen-nx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:58:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] nx: memory limit, hang diagnostics and test hooks

- debug.SetMemoryLimit at 80% of the fixed Go heap block: the GC does not
  know about the cap and let garbage run it out (Go OOM on big games).
- Log Go heap and frame rate every 10 s; a Horizon watchdog thread and a
  goroutine dump when the main loop stalls; loader step traces.
- Optional args.txt next to the .nro with Ikemen command line flags, plus
  -nxautokeys[=N], -nxpreloadall, -nxheapprofile and -nxconsolelog for
  testing in the emulator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
